# %% [markdown]
# # DriftSense — 05: Anomaly Detection Engine & Calibration
#
# **Runtime Type:** Python 3 (CPU or GPU)  
# **Estimated Runtime:** ~1-3 minutes  
# **RAM Needed:** ~2-4 GB  
# **Disk Needed:** ~1 GB  
# **Expected Outputs:**  
# - Detector Checkpoints: `runs/<run_id>/models/{zscore,rolling_threshold,iforest,ocsvm}.joblib`  
# - Validation Detections Matrix: `runs/<run_id>/val_detections.csv`  
# - Validation Detection Metrics Report: `runs/<run_id>/val_detect_metrics.json`  
# - Synthetic Ground-Truth Labels (Contract 6): `runs/<run_id>/val_anomaly_labels.json`  
# - Operational Events Table (Contract 5): `runs/<run_id>/val_operational_events.json`  
# - Detection Visualizations: `runs/<run_id>/detection_comparison.png`  
# - Cryptographically Verified Manifest: `runs/<run_id>/manifest.json`  
#
# > **CRITICAL EVALUATION & ISOLATION INVARIANTS (G6 & A7.3):**  
# > - **Independent Ground Truth (Contract 9):** Anomaly ground truth is established independently via Contract 6 and Contract 9, never inferred from detector output.  
# > - **Dual Track Separation:** Results are partitioned into Real Data Track (evaluating false positive rates across normal diurnal and weekend regimes) and Synthetic Track (evaluating Precision, Recall, Event-F1, and temporal detection delay).  
# > - **A7.3 Test Quarantine:** The test partition ($D_{\text{test}}$, Days 25–30) is strictly locked. No detections are generated or evaluated on test data.

